Arduino sketch includes void setup() and void loop(). Without them, your program won&#8217;t run!<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The code that you put inside\u00a0void setup() will only run once, and that will be at the beginning of your program. One example is when you want to turn your robot on &#8212; that does not happen multiple times!<\/li>\n<li>In void loop(), your code will repeat over and over again. Examples are when your robot is driving or using its sensor to check for obstacles.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Short version: code in\u00a0void setup() runs once and code in void loop() runs for-ev-er.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1322&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 4 Briefing video [vc_column_text]If you need more visuals for the Arduino Functions lesson, this video is for you![\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=ELbN8gAs_BE\" align=\"center\"] [\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column] Step 5 What are functions? [vc_column_text]Programs can&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/arduino-functions\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1732,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"easy","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":802,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[626,1533,1438,144,171,209],"lesson-tag":[2163,2213,2174,2131,2118,2122,2172,2171,2214],"class_list":["post-1321","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-arduino-function","lesson-tag-coding","lesson-tag-functions","lesson-tag-loops","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-robotics","lesson-tag-rokit-smart","lesson-tag-setup","module-programming","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/les